{"classified_as":[{"_id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300033799","label":"oil paintings (visual works)","type":"Type"},{"_id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300033618","label":"paintings (visual works)","type":"Type"},{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/object/8604","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":"8604","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"non-preferred identifiers","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300264273"}],"content":"530, Catalogue Raisonné","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"catalogue raisonnée number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026061"}],"content":"530","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"non-preferred identifiers","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300264273"}],"content":{"alternate-title":{"titles":[{"notes":"Source of title: Museum of Fine Arts, St. Petersburg.","title":"New York – Night (Madison Avenue)","type":"alternate-title"}],"type":"alternate-title"},"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne":{"titles":[{"notes":"Source of title: Downtown Gallery Archive.","title":"Madison Avenue","type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}],"type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"},"selected-exhibition-titles":{"titles":["New York - Night\nViews of the City, 2000, Georgia O'Keeffe Museum (Santa Fe)"],"type":"selected-exhibition-titles"},"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne":{"titles":[{"notes":"Source of title: Whitney Archive, Abiquiú Notebooks.","title":"New York – Night","type":"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}],"type":"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}},"type":"Name"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"New York – Night","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"Georgia O'Keeffe","id":"actor/2","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Measurement Description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/measurement_description"}],"content":"32 1/2 x 12 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Holding Institution","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_instituion"}],"content":"Museum of Fine Arts, St. Petersburg","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Title and Date","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_title_date"}],"content":"New York – Night, 1926","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"credit line","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026687"}],"content":"Gift of Charles C. \u0026 Margaret Stevenson Henderson in memory of Hunt Henderson","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Materials description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/materials_description"}],"content":"Oil on canvas","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Medium and Dimensions","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_medium_dims"}],"content":"Oil on canvas, 32 1/2 x 12 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"cr_remarks_1999","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/cr_remarks_1999"}],"content":["Hunt Henderson owned this work and *Red Poppy* (see cat. entry 638), according to his heirs. Yet entries in Whitney Archive and Abiquiú Notebooks associate Henderson with *New York – Night*, a 1927 painting, which was no. 1 in the 1928 New York (Intimate Gallery) checklist. Neither entry included measurements for the piece originally, but at some point Doris Bry wrote '48 x 30'into the Abiquiú Notebooks entry. The painting owned by Henderson measures 32 x 12. Downtown Gallery Archive titles the Henderson painting 'Madison Avenue, 1926'and indicates that Henderson purchased it from the Intimate Gallery. In 1929 letters from Stieglitz to Henderson that refer to his purchases, Stieglitz wrote; 'She [O'Keeffe] is delighted that you are to have the white abstraction with the wild red picture you have of her's'(22 March 1929, museum files); 'Did I ever acknowledge your kind letter of May 22 in which you tell me that the paintings arrived [an O'Keeffe and a Marin] and how you enjoyed particularly the white O'Keeffe\" (30 October 1929, museum files). And in a 1955 letter to Edith Halpert, O'Keeffe mentions both paintings purchased by Henderson: \"One [New York painting] that! think would be very good to have [for an exhibition Halpert had written her about] was owned by a New Orleans Sugar man named Henderson. He also had a large Red Poppy. The *N.Y Night 27* is an abstract thing—very simple—and I think very good\" (O'Keeffe to Edith Halpert, 7 May 1955, Archive of American Art). Because the painting was exhibited in 1928 and listed as *New York—Night* on the Intimate Gallery checklist, O'Keeffe and Irvine titled it as such and dated it 1927, as the painting was not available for examination. This date error was repeated in Abiquiú Notebooks. How the work came to be titled *Madison Avenue* in Downtown Gallery Archive is unclear. (Source: Lynes, 1999)"],"type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Complete","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_complete"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe. New York – Night, 1926. Oil on canvas, 32 1/2 x 12 inches. Museum of Fine Arts, St. Petersburg. Gift of Charles C. \u0026 Margaret Stevenson Henderson in memory of Hunt Henderson. © Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"provenance_narrative","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/provenance_narrative"}],"content":"(The Intimate Gallery, New York, NY); sold to Hunt Henderson [1872–1939], New Orleans, LA, before March 22, 1929; by descent to Charles C. [1920–2016] and Margaret S. Henderson [d. 1980], New Orleans, LA; given to the Museum of Fine Arts, St. Petersburg, FL, June 14, 1971. \n(Source: Museum of Fine Arts, St. Petersburg, 2025)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"In this semiabstract composition, lines spring from a point on the lefthand side of the work, interrupting a smooth, white surface. A band of color runs diagonally from the bottom left to the top right of the work and transitions from bluish-white at the bottom to bright yellow at the top.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Copyright","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_copyright"}],"content":"© Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Artist(s)","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_artist"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[{"digitally_shown_by":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/863341/full/full/0/default.jpg","type":"DigitalObject"}],"classified_as":[{"_label":"Digital Image","id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300215302","type":"Type"}],"digitally_available_via":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/863341"}],"conforms_to":[{"id":"http://iiif.io/api/image","type":"InformationObject"}],"format":"application/ld+json;profile='http://iiif.io/api/image/2/context.json'","type":"DigitalService"}],"type":"DigitalObject"}],"type":"VisualItem"}],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}